  "summary": "DIR-100 plan (re-scoped by RCA). The director targeted RU-001 (* catch-all, NOT_EXECUTED, not remediable). Root-cause analysis of the REAL outstanding units (RU-002 /, RU-029 /features, RU-032 /jobs/browse, RU-033 /jobs/categories, RU-039 /login, RU-047 /portfolios, all 96-97) found they failed the SAME two a11y checks - heading (h1 != 1) and landmark-nav (no nav landmark) - which are FALSE POSITIVES. Evidence: a probe reproducing the audit sequence showed h1=0 and nav=0 at the FIRST viewport (320px) immediately after navigation, but h1=1 and nav=1 at 375px+. The audit probed the 320px viewport before the SPA finished rendering. FIX: scripts/ux-audit.mjs now waits for primary content (h1/main/nav) to render before probing. RESULT after re-audit: 46/46 auditable units ACCEPTED at >=98/100 (was 40/58), avg 98/100, 0 P0/P1 defects. The 12 remaining units are parameterised routes (/blog/:slug, /jobs/portal/:jobId, /shared/:resumeId, ...) that require real record data to audit - documented BLOCKED, not failed. Acceptance: all auditable units >=98; audit render-race fixed; no fabrication."
